  "solution": {
    "text": "Inter-molecular structure of Boric acid(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>BO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>) in solid phase:<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0022_88dec3c6b381.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 270px;\" /><br />Boric acid has strong hydrogen bonding as we can see in the above figure, while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;does not. Therefore boric acid is solid."
